.TITLE "cls"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Clears the command prompt window. It removes all text from the screen and positions the cursor at the top-left corner of the __console buffer__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**cls**
Clears the entire screen of the active command prompt window.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Running __cls__ is a simple way to reset your visual workspace after executing commands with high-volume output. It only clears the visible screen and does not affect the command history or environment variables.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:echo** **windows:dir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/cls__
